  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Cani Plouf occupies the Crique du Moulin, at the left end of Garonne beach in Le Pradet: a secluded spot, away from swimmers and boaters, presented by the Provence Méditerranée tourist office as a space for dogs and their owners. The tourist office classes the site as a "rock beach", on the outskirts of town and less than ten minutes' walk from a bus stop. Access is free and open every day of the year.</p>
      <p>The local press (actu.fr, April 2025) reports that the town inaugurated "Cani Plouf" on 7 April 2025, described by the mayor as an "isolated strip of beach" and presented as the first beach in the Var entirely dedicated to dogs, in the presence of the Diverti chiens dog club. The busiest beaches remain closed to dogs, according to the same article.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The tourist office specifies that animals are accompanied by their owners, who see to hygiene rules. It adds that, apart from Cani Plouf, dogs on a leash are tolerated on Le Pradet's other beaches from 1 November to 31 March. According to the press, signs on site recall the rules: second-category dogs must be muzzled and on a leash, and first-category dogs are banned.</p>
      <p>On the town hall's side, a permanent order no. 2025-ARR-PM-PERM-090 on the presence of animals on beaches, dated 4 April 2025, is published on the town's website; its text could not be read in full. The permanent 2022 order, for its part, bans dogs, even on a leash, from beaches and coves from 1 May to 31 October, with a leash compulsory the rest of the year. The Garonne beach listing also states that access for any animal, even on a leash, is banned there. These texts do not match the presentation of the cove: call the town hall (04 94 08 69 47) before coming, especially out of season, and do not swim anywhere other than the dedicated cove.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: outside the Crique du Moulin, assume Le Pradet's beaches are closed to dogs, unless the town hall confirms otherwise. Bring fresh water and bags: the site is isolated.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Le Pradet's coastal path is nearby, but the town hall reports that the stretch between Garonne beach and Bonnettes beach remains closed to pedestrians.</p>
